Additional terms and provenance notes
-------------------------------------

1. Source data. SEER-Bench is derived from coded fields in a versioned release
   of the SEER Research Data, obtained under a signed SEER data-use agreement.
   The released items are natural-language clinical vignettes synthesized from
   those coded fields together with gold labels taken directly from the coded
   staging variables. They are not SEER patient records and contain no
   identifiers. Users remain responsible for complying with the SEER data-use
   terms that apply to them.

2. Guideline sources. The training corpora are rendered from clinical update
   events identified in the NCCN Guidelines(R) and related expert consensus
   documents. The released items are paraphrased clinical questions and
   rationales; they do not reproduce guideline text verbatim. Use of the
   underlying guidelines remains subject to the NCCN Guidelines(R) terms of use.

3. Intended use. These artifacts are intended for research on medical knowledge
   updating and for benchmarking. They are not intended for, and must not be
   used as, a basis for diagnosis, staging, treatment, or medication decisions
   without qualified clinical oversight.
